{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209634-terrestrial-vs-celestial-how-big-is-the-power-gap-now","id":1209634,"title":"Terrestrial VS Celestial: How big is the power gap now?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-21T08:12:13-07:00","id":1209634,"title":"Terrestrial VS Celestial: How big is the power gap now?","content":"I have happily backed the dragonblooded kickstarter and have been thrilled with everything I have read so far. I am incredibly impressed with the manuscript so far, and have tons of confidence in the new dev team.However I haven't had as much time to sit and tinker with the new Charms as I would like, and was wondering what the wise minds of this forum might think about them. <br /> <br /> So how big is the power gap between Solars and Dragonblooded now? Could something like an Essence 3 Dynast be a deadly threat to a newborn Dawn? Are the 2e days of combat specced Solars laughing in the face of dozens of Wyld Hunters long gone?<br /> <br /> Eager to hear peoples thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T08:36:28-07:00","id":1209645,"title":"","content":"It's kind of a hard question to answer, since there isn't exactly a unit in which one can measure power gaps...<br /> <br /> \u200bAcross the board, Dragon Blooded are still weaker. For one thing, their mote pools and dice caps are smaller, and for the latter, they need to buy the Charms rather than just having the Abilities. Anima powers are generally less extreme. And there are certain big ticket events, such as shaping the Wyld or grappling gigantic enemies that they don't get.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat they have that might compare to Solars is less powerful, but not insignificant. They also have a number of powers that, in the actual use of them, are very strong, some at least as strong as what an effect laid down by a Solar might be. But several require a lot of setup, such as big Initiative leads or having one's Aura prepared, and can only be used once per time interval with either no reset condition, or fairly big ones. The Aura mechanic itself presents a principle in which a number of powerful Charms are incompatible, or one might be prematurely ended by using even a minor Charm from another Ability. Approaching a Solar might require some care, assuming that they've gotten some Essence 3 or 4 Charms in a Supernal that can be applied dangerously. They've also got the often powerful Signature Charms, in which buying one means not being any of the four others.<br /> <br /> \u200bHowever, they do have a few things that compensate them for this a bit. Quite a few more Charms to give them dice or successes that don't count against their cap, as well as several to provide temporary specialties to help increase their cap. Plus some of the benefits they can get from Sworn Kin in a few Charms.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Dragon Blooded have a few methods for punching above their weight class, it just costs them in a few ways or requires them to apply their powers carefully.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Also, with Artifacts, they've got some good stuff for making them, but that will have a difficult time with anything above a certain level; at the same time, the Artifacts that they're actually in possession of already can also help them gain some powers above their usual standard)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T08:41:47-07:00","id":1209648,"title":"","content":"Of course, an Essence 3 Dynast be a threat to a Dawn, but it also depends on how much investment each of them has in his combat charms. If the Dawn is something like 12 charms in Melee or Brawl with 3 Ox Bodies he will still go through the E3 DB quite easily, but if you assume that having 3-4 Melee charms you will not die versus a combat focused DB you are in for a rude awakening.<br /> <br /> Also, one versus twelve at least at E1 is impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T09:58:56-07:00","id":1209674,"title":"","content":"A few scattered thoughts:<br /> <br /> Among relatively young Exalts, any dragon-blooded who can survive the Solar's big essence spend is going to have some advantages in a long fight. Their excellencies have to be purchased, sure, but they come with free dice tricks. Those little edges in efficiency that shouldn't be dismissed. A Solar who can afford to buy and use scenelong effects is probably going to overwhelm that advantage.<br /> <br /> The deadliest Dawn I've ever actually played could probably kill two, maaaybe three members of a Wyld Hunt before going down, but she'd definitely go down The nature of decisive attacks (extra successes don't matter, if you have the init and you hit, they're screwed) strongly favors raw maximum dice pool in a fair fight between peers. The inherent swinginess of the dice system means that same gap isn't enough to save you from numbers, and Solar charms aren't so mighty as to give outright immunity to attacks (unlike first edition).<br /> <br /> Running third edition somewhat casually, I've learned there's two modes most Solar PCs operate in: casual essence expenditures, and balls-to-the-wall defining character moments. An Exalt can get a lot done with only four motes of essence per action, which is what it takes to spend peripheral essence without bumping up their animas. When PCs go all out, they spend everything they can for a moment where the actual dice roll is almost a perfunctory formality, either openly flaring or dumping their entire personal pool.<br /> <br /> In that context, consider the Dragon-Blooded. Within their specialty, they will spend more than four motes at a time, because their anima is strictly an asset outside of fragile environments. Their defining moments might have a slightly smaller dice cap by default, but they can probably make up the EV with the free dice tricks and with their big scary signature charms. I imagine they are close enough in utility for a mixed circle to work just fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T10:02:42-07:00","id":1209676,"title":"","content":"Does anyone else feel that the DB social charms are much closer in power/utility to Solar ones than the DB combat, craft, stealth, etc, charms?<br /> <br /> They seem to have a lot more charms where I go &quot;hmmm, that'd actually be really useful&quot;, like a number of charms instilling Major intimacies, and a fair few charms for instilling/inspiring that require Decision Points to resist rather than just a WP. Mostly I'm talking about Presence, but a bit in other abilities as well.<br /> They're much less likely to be able to get the extremely high amount of successes Solars can get, admittedly (our Zenith sometimes gets 20+ when preaching), but sometimes with Solar social characters, in my experience, they're easily able to throw 12+ successes at you (nearly always enough to break your Resolve), but this tends to just lead to people spending WP.<br /> <br /> Whereas with other charm trees, I can definitely see how they're weaker than a similarly-built Solar.<br /> <br /> (Also, Aura can be a minor thing or quite awkward, depending on your build. I was looking at the Water signature charm in Melee, which is brutal, and there's a couple of other fun Water charms in Melee, but I can't really see any good way to get into Water Aura without making Brawl attacks for a round or something.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T10:49:01-07:00","id":1209691,"title":"","content":"It's quite fitting, really. Dragon Blooded are big on families and community. They don't have the sheer divine, world-shaping might that the celestial exalted can muster, but they are good at management and dealing with people directly in a way that lofty old solars might be a tad lacking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T10:53:39-07:00","id":1209693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209634-terrestrial-vs-celestial-how-big-is-the-power-gap-now?p=1209676#post1209676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Aura can be a minor thing or quite awkward, depending on your build. I was looking at the Water signature charm in Melee, which is brutal, and there's a couple of other fun Water charms in Melee, but I can't really see any good way to get into Water Aura without making Brawl attacks for a round or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you remember that any Aura you're in automatically changes to match your Aspect when your anima banner goes iconic?<br /> <br /> That's currently the only way that a Terrestrial Brawler can access the Air or Fire Signature Charms without using Charms from another Ability or their anima powers. The Air or Fire Aspect needs to use the Water Charms to enter Water Aura, and burn enough motes to take their anima to iconic, which gives them the Air or Fire Aura necessary to execute their Signature Super Attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T10:59:00-07:00","id":1209695,"title":"","content":"That's true, so I suppose you could attack with the melee excellency the first turn, going into fire aura, and if by the time you've reached your next turn if you've spent enough motes to get to iconic you could switch to water aura. Not very easy, but it works. And those charms are the sort that you probably don't want to use on the first turn anyway (like doubling your decisive damage, you probably want to get in at least one withering attack first).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T11:56:53-07:00","id":1209715,"title":"","content":"I think this is the first time that Exalted's meta-game has demanded a FLOW CHART.<br /> <br /> MULTIPLE flow charts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T11:57:02-07:00","id":1209716,"title":"","content":"You could also use the air brawl signature by using Soaring Leap Technique to disengage the turn before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T12:03:33-07:00","id":1209718,"title":"","content":"Naturally, the Air Signature Melee and Brawl Charms can be used after establishing and maintaining concealment with Air Stealth Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T12:25:35-07:00","id":1209730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209634-terrestrial-vs-celestial-how-big-is-the-power-gap-now?p=1209715#post1209715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is the first time that Exalted's meta-game has demanded a FLOW CHART.<br /> <br /> MULTIPLE flow charts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sort of chuckling that a Fire-Aspected unarmed combatant has a flow chart. Of course, much like Limit, it's not the same kind of thing as in <a href=\"http://knowyourmeme.com/memes/flowchart-ken\" target=\"_blank\">the video game</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T13:04:23-07:00","id":1209751,"title":"","content":"For Water Melee in particular, the first <i>four</i> Charms in Melee are all Balanced, which seems generous compared to a lot of the trees.<br /> <br /> Air is still the Aura I'm most concerned about, since there are <i>ver</i><i>y</i> few defensive Air Charms, particularly within the reach of starting characters. I guess they'll just have to lean on Excellencies or Martial Arts on defense for the most part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T13:36:36-07:00","id":1209760,"title":"","content":"Hmm.<br /> <br /> Tempting as it seemed, it is not actually possible to chain Steel Tempest Strike into Mela's Flashing Tongue <i>with </i>Air Aura for a second decisive attack. They made sure you need to spend Air Aura to use Steel Tempest Strike, which means you can't access the full power of Mela's Flashing Tongue in the same round... unless someone uses a Charm from the Air-heavy Lore tree to grant you their Air Aura.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T13:37:40-07:00","id":1209761,"title":"","content":"True, but if you're using archery your best defence is for other people to be up close to the enemy while you're far away and don't have to worry about it.<br /> <br /> Not a perfect method of course, but what is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T13:43:02-07:00","id":1209765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209634-terrestrial-vs-celestial-how-big-is-the-power-gap-now?p=1209761#post1209761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but if you're using archery your best defence is for other people to be up close to the enemy while you're far away and don't have to worry about it.<br /> <br /> Not a perfect method of course, but what is?</div> </div> </div> </div>...I'm talking about Melee Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T14:40:30-07:00","id":1209780,"title":"","content":"You Ninja'd me, my response was to Ascension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T14:52:34-07:00","id":1209782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ascension</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209634-terrestrial-vs-celestial-how-big-is-the-power-gap-now?p=1209751#post1209751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Air is still the Aura I'm most concerned about, since there are <i>ver</i><i>y</i> few defensive Air Charms, particularly within the reach of starting characters. I guess they'll just have to lean on Excellencies or Martial Arts on defense for the most part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you can use Stealth Charms, most of which are Air.<br /> <br /> Air is the stealthy element, so it only makes sense that the Signature attacks available to Air Aspects work best as surprise attacks that rely upon Air's stealthiness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T16:05:13-07:00","id":1209800,"title":"","content":"<br /> Off the top of my head, Dragon-Blooded are set below Solar Exalts by...<ul><li>Smaller dice pools and lower dice caps</li> <li>No free excellencies</li> <li>Terrestrial and Mastery</li> <li>Aura</li> <li>Charms that are narrower in scope, more limited in use (reset conditions), lesser in magnitude</li> <li>Lack of 3E-style perfects</li> <li>XP levels for Essence</li> <li>As I recall, there was at least one instance (maybe more) of fails-against-magic</li> <li>DB fiction usually seems to involve a loss for every win, whereas the Solar fiction mostly involves clowning people left and right</li> <li>(While not part of the calculation, they also lost some of the things from previous editions that helped to mitigate a bit of this, at least for a while, like superior artifact backgrounds and more skill points from a life of rigorous education.)</li> </ul>That's a lot of work put into the power gap; and the gap strikes me as quite large. The lack of free excellencies feels like an exalted competence gap, which I've found to be kind of rough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":415,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","user":"Equitable Remedy","date":". 04-21-2018, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","name":"Equitable Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T16:14:29-07:00","id":1209805,"title":"","content":"Solars with a combat supernal stand a decent chance of going 5v1 with DBs still. The Heaven Sword Flash combo lets you wipe out a whole circle in a white room before they can even act, or at least enough of them to end the combat. DBs also don't have any of the insane damage boosting charms that Solars have, which means they're going to struggle peeling initiative out of one who's got a good soak and armor. They also have a tendency to have some of their more devastating effects locked behind things like needing 15+ initiative, or getting attacked a bunch of times but not being hit. Which against a Dawn is really unlikely to happen.<br /> <br /> Don't let any of this make you think DBs aren't powerful though, it's just that certain Solars are VERY powerful. Most Solar exalted, and even a good chunk of the more fighty ones, do not want to engage in a 5v1 against Dragonblooded. At essence 3 when the DBs have their signature charms even a 1v1 against an essence 1 Solar is dangerous. Where DBs really shine though is fighting things that aren't Solars. Gods, elementals, things that don't have the stuff like Fivefold Bulwark Stance, those are the people that really fear DBs.<br /> <br /> I will also say that it's definitely possible for a Wyld Hunt to fight even a very powerful Solar, which wasn't always true for 2e. You just need to be smart, sacrifice a lot, and wear them down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T16:46:39-07:00","id":1209813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209634-terrestrial-vs-celestial-how-big-is-the-power-gap-now?p=1209805#post1209805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will also say that it's definitely possible for a Wyld Hunt to fight even a very powerful Solar, which wasn't always true for 2e. You just need to be smart, sacrifice a lot, and wear them down.</div> </div> </div> </div>I expect this to be the big difference. There was a point in 2e when DBs stopped being a threat, albeit a very high optimization-wise. Below it, however, Dragon-Blooded of superior Essence and gear could challenge even well-built Solar circles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","name":"emeraldstreak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1628_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T16:49:12-07:00","id":1209814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209634-terrestrial-vs-celestial-how-big-is-the-power-gap-now?p=1209761#post1209761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but if you're using archery your best defence is for other people to be up close to the enemy while you're far away and don't have to worry about it.<br /> <br /> Not a perfect method of course, but what is?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209634-terrestrial-vs-celestial-how-big-is-the-power-gap-now?p=1209782#post1209782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you can use Stealth Charms, most of which are Air.<br /> <br /> Air is the stealthy element, so it only makes sense that the Signature attacks available to Air Aspects work best as surprise attacks that rely upon Air's stealthiness.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Ninja&quot; and &quot;Archer&quot; are both very specific builds, and neither explains a character like, say, Tepet Arada.<br /> <br /> Actually, it'll be very interesting to see how Arada is statted in Heirs to the Shogunate, since he does now canonically have two Solar kills in melee combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T16:57:16-07:00","id":1209817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ascension</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209634-terrestrial-vs-celestial-how-big-is-the-power-gap-now?p=1209814#post1209814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Ninja&quot; and &quot;Archer&quot; are both very specific builds, and neither explains a character like, say, Tepet Arada.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tepet Arada doesn't need Air Aura for any Melee Charm besides Steel Tempest Strike, and he can get an Air Aura by having any Aura at all when he reaches iconic anima flare.<br /> <br /> He might not even know Steel Tempest Strike, but instead have chosen one of the other four Melee Signature Charms. Unless he's Essence 5, he wouldn't qualify to learn a second.<br /> <br /> Mela's Flashing Tongue is the only other Air-aspected Melee Charm, and it doesn't require Air Aura for anything but a little extra power that you don't always want to use, anyway.<br /> <br /> Elemental Sheath and Dragon-Graced Weapon, as well as his own Air Aspect anima powers, can also be used to achieve Air Aura, especially since so many basic Melee Charms are Balanced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T17:18:46-07:00","id":1209827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ascension</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209634-terrestrial-vs-celestial-how-big-is-the-power-gap-now?p=1209814#post1209814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Ninja&quot; and &quot;Archer&quot; are both very specific builds, and neither explains a character like, say, Tepet Arada.<br /> <br /> Actually, it'll be very interesting to see how Arada is statted in Heirs to the Shogunate, since he does now canonically have two Solar kills in melee combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not on his own. There's a tremendous difference in the combat capability required to fight a duel against a fully prepped and ready combat-oriented Solar and what's required to finish one off after he's blown all his essence and initiative on your friends. Not that Arada isn't a badass who would threaten a Solar 1v1, but the circumstances of those fights are pretty important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T17:41:01-07:00","id":1209835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209634-terrestrial-vs-celestial-how-big-is-the-power-gap-now?p=1209800#post1209800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]As I recall, there was at least one instance (maybe more) of fails-against-magic</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bCan you recall it specifically?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">like superior artifact backgrounds</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat raises a question to me; what were those extra dots spent on? It seems to me that it wasn't worth having more than one daiklave, and a lot of other possible stuff provided relatively minor benefits.<br /> <br /> \u200bMaybe Dragon Blooded don't get a bunch of amulets and things on the side when they spend three dots to get a daiklave, but that daiklave is far more impressive than in previous Editions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a lot of work put into the power gap; and the gap strikes me as quite large</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it was always going to be. I feel as though some of this might be the kind of thing that I was warning against when I suggested to a few people to temper their expectations of what a reduced power gap meant.<br /> <br /> \u200bEven if the power gap is large, I think that it cannot be denied that there are some impressive Charms in there, and that the overall system affords means of not being made rapidly insignificant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lack of free excellencies feels like an exalted competence gap, which I've found to be kind of rough.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> I'm not entirely sure what is meant by &quot;exalted competence gap&quot; here.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T18:02:37-07:00","id":1209840,"title":"","content":"The larceny charm that lets you turn into water to flow though cracks and stuff also lets you escape from a grapple, but it has to be a non-magically-assisted grapple. <br /> <br /> So it does have &quot;fails against magic&quot; for a side benefit of a charm in a non-combat ability. What I <i>don't</i> think there is are any actual defensive charms whose entire purpose is negated by a single mote spent on an excellency. And that's the shit that needed to go. So on the whole, we're good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T18:08:48-07:00","id":1209842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209634-terrestrial-vs-celestial-how-big-is-the-power-gap-now?p=1209840#post1209840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So it does have &quot;fails against magic&quot; for a side benefit of a charm in a non-combat ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAnd I'm inclined to view that more as a capacity of magic to enhance grapples than a flaw in the power of the Charm. That the logic of that one goes &quot;of course, they can't grapple you, you're made of water&quot;, but if you should encounter somebody who <i>can</i> grapple water, the wind, time or God, then you're not going to slip away just because.<br /> <br /> \u200b(I'm being poetic there, please nobody bother me with ideas of whether or not any given Charm should specify the mythic scope of its grappling)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T18:42:18-07:00","id":1209847,"title":"","content":"It's really no different from how Blazing Solar Bolt can't be evaded or parried without spending one mote on an Excellency, or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T18:54:46-07:00","id":1209851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209634-terrestrial-vs-celestial-how-big-is-the-power-gap-now?p=1209847#post1209847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's really no different from how Blazing Solar Bolt can't be evaded or parried without spending one mote on an Excellency, or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except insofar as it was liberally applied in 2e to where entire combat charm suites were negated by 1m attack or defense. (hyperbole yes but still).<br /> <br /> The fact that it isn't being spread like marmite all over the DB charmset is a major improvement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T19:06:37-07:00","id":1209859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209634-terrestrial-vs-celestial-how-big-is-the-power-gap-now?p=1209851#post1209851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except insofar as it was liberally applied in 2e to where entire combat charm suites were negated by 1m attack or defense. (hyperbole yes but still).<br /> <br /> The fact that it isn't being spread like marmite all over the DB charmset is a major improvement.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was referring specifically to the clause Elfive mentioned for the new Larceny Charm.<br /> <br /> I wasn't dismissing how much past editions of Portentous Comet Deflection were embarrassingly badly designed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T01:37:41-07:00","id":1209944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209634-terrestrial-vs-celestial-how-big-is-the-power-gap-now?p=1209817#post1209817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elemental Sheath and Dragon-Graced Weapon, as well as his own Air Aspect anima powers, can also be used to achieve Air Aura, especially since so many basic Melee Charms are Balanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Elemental Sheath and Dragon-Graced Weapon have no keywords, they're not &quot;Air <i>or</i> Earth <i>or</i> Fire <i>or</i> Water <i>or</i> Wood&quot; which I'd expect.<br /> <br /> Same with Elemental Bolt, and a few others with 5 different versions.<br /> <br /> Which seems very odd, so I wondered if I'm missing something?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That raises a question to me; what were those extra dots spent on? It seems to me that it wasn't worth having more than one daiklave, and a lot of other possible stuff provided relatively minor benefits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally, in my experience, a lot of people would spend 3 dots of artefacts and get a daiklaive, hearthstone bracers, and magic armour.<br /> <br /> (Well, quite frequently people would get 2 daiklaives, they'd get 2 short daiklaives because Jade Short Daiklaives were Speed 3 and thus amazing, but that's the same cost as one regular Daiklaive so probably doesn't count.)<br /> <br /> But the particular benefit of having a better Artefact background no longer existing is mitigated by the fact that a starting Solar has 10 merits, while a starting Dynast has18 merits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>(While not part of the calculation, they also lost some of the things from previous editions that helped to mitigate a bit of this, at least for a while, like superior artifact backgrounds and more skill points from a life of rigorous education.)</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">So, while I agree with most of your points, I think that now starting Dynasts get 1 more specialisation, 1 more essence, 3 more freebies, and 8 more Merits (nearly twice as many) is slightly better than that.<br /> I'd say the main thing they had in 2nd ed that mitigated this, which they no longer have, is their dirt cheap excellencies (which got cheaper in 2.5) and their free reflexives. Which isn't an issue now, but needing to spend that WP for combos was a big disadvantage for Solars which DBs didn't have to worry about. <br /> I remember once our 40xp Solars+Lunars fought a single Fire Aspect. We had almost no artefacts (one guy had god-kicking boots), he had a Dire Lance and Five-Dragon Force Blow (the single charm responsible for the most PC casualties in games I played), artefact armour, and an optimised build, unlike any of us. It took all of us to beat him, and he seriously screwed us up doing so. After that, we were actually terrified of fighting Dragonblood, and... basically never did it. We ended up fleeing the Wyld Hunt 3 times. (Whereas most games I played, PCs beat the Wyld Hunt a couple of times and then are so far beyond them they don't care).<br /> <br /> But of course, Solars have much weaker charms now, which is the big mitigator.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T02:22:29-07:00","id":1209956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209634-terrestrial-vs-celestial-how-big-is-the-power-gap-now?p=1209800#post1209800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>Lack of 3E-style perfects</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>What they've got is really close in some places. I mean I'd be lying if I said I wasn't a bit concerned by the lack of options for dealing with Uncountable Damage because I'm worried that in the future some idiot is going to put that on a charm or spell and restore the old paradigm of &quot;when I learn this Dragon-Blooded simply aren't a threat to me anymore&quot;.<br /> <br /> But then, it's also easy to overwhelm Seven Shadow Evasion if the Storyteller is malicious enough.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T02:36:39-07:00","id":1209958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209634-terrestrial-vs-celestial-how-big-is-the-power-gap-now?p=1209944#post1209944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elemental Sheath and Dragon-Graced Weapon have no keywords, they're not &quot;Air <i>or</i> Earth <i>or</i> Fire <i>or</i> Water <i>or</i> Wood&quot; which I'd expect.<br /> <br /> Same with Elemental Bolt, and a few others with 5 different versions.<br /> <br /> Which seems very odd, so I wondered if I'm missing something?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Elemental Bolt Attack mentions that it shares an aspect with the exalt (and presumably the variants change to match their own type). There's no such line in the text of Elemental Sheath though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T07:55:39-07:00","id":1210026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209634-terrestrial-vs-celestial-how-big-is-the-power-gap-now?p=1209944#post1209944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elemental Sheath and Dragon-Graced Weapon have no keywords, they're not &quot;Air <i>or</i> Earth <i>or</i> Fire <i>or</i> Water <i>or</i> Wood&quot; which I'd expect.<br /> <br /> Same with Elemental Bolt, and a few others with 5 different versions.<br /> <br /> Which seems very odd, so I wondered if I'm missing something?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209634-terrestrial-vs-celestial-how-big-is-the-power-gap-now?p=1209958#post1209958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elemental Bolt Attack mentions that it shares an aspect with the exalt (and presumably the variants change to match their own type). There's no such line in the text of Elemental Sheath though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wizard asked Robert what he intended.<br /> <br /> Robert confirmed that Elemental Sheath/Dragon-Graced Weapon and the five-fold, unkeyworded Resistance Charms all effectively have the elemental keyword appropriate to the element you invoke/use.<br /> <br /> Also that EBA indeed has the aspect of the element you throw at people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T17:36:23-07:00","id":1210194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209634-terrestrial-vs-celestial-how-big-is-the-power-gap-now?p=1209817#post1209817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and he can get an Air Aura by having any Aura at all when he reaches iconic anima flare...</div> </div> </div> </div>While that's true for <i>reaching</i> your Aspect aura, I've seen no indication that you can't be knocked <i>out </i>of your Aspect aura in bonfire. Bonfire's more of a liability than an asset when it comes to maintaining Aura, IMO, though that may be a necessary balance on the power of Anima Flux, along with a reinforcement of Aspect identity.<br /> <br /> Eh. I'm probably fretting too much over Air's defenses. The weakness of Dragon-Blooded defense penalty negators across the board is a pretty clear indication that their basic defenses simply aren't supposed to be that strong, and in that environment leaning on Excellencies and the small number of Balanced Charms like Flame-Borne Interception for defense at Character Creation might not be as much of a liability as I've been imagining it to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T18:13:42-07:00","id":1210203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209634-terrestrial-vs-celestial-how-big-is-the-power-gap-now?p=1209800#post1209800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Off the top of my head, Dragon-Blooded are set below Solar Exalts by...<ul><li>Smaller dice pools and lower dice caps</li> <li>No free excellencies</li> <li>Terrestrial and Mastery</li> <li>Aura</li> <li>Charms that are narrower in scope, more limited in use (reset conditions), lesser in magnitude</li> <li>Lack of 3E-style perfects</li> <li>XP levels for Essence</li> <li>As I recall, there was at least one instance (maybe more) of fails-against-magic</li> <li><b>DB fiction usually seems to involve a loss for every win, whereas the Solar fiction mostly involves clowning people left and right</b></li> <li>(While not part of the calculation, they also lost some of the things from previous editions that helped to mitigate a bit of this, at least for a while, like superior artifact backgrounds and more skill points from a life of rigorous education.)</li> </ul><br /> That's a lot of work put into the power gap; and the gap strikes me as quite large. The lack of free excellencies feels like an exalted competence gap, which I've found to be kind of rough.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The first one was basically there to stress how important team work is and make it stick to the player that you definitely want to form a sworn brotherhood on top of regular teamwork. Once they actually started doing it right they whooped ass and dragged one of them back to the Scarlet Empress as a drugged up chakra skewered meat sack for her to do whatever secret thing she did with solars. Mnemon also made off pretty well, she took damage but drove Nova off and had her forces (including a demon that lives in her blood or something weird like that) hunting her down. None of them really made them look bad outside the first one deliberately showing why you shouldn't be a scrub and refuse to form that awesome magical bond with your team if you don't want to get crushed by celestial's superior one to one power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T18:15:50-07:00","id":1210204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ascension</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209634-terrestrial-vs-celestial-how-big-is-the-power-gap-now?p=1210194#post1210194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While that's true for <i>reaching</i> your Aspect aura, I've seen no indication that you can't be knocked <i>out </i>of your Aspect aura in bonfire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good catch.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bonfire's more of a liability than an asset when it comes to maintaining Aura, IMO, though that may be a necessary balance on the power of Anima Flux, along with a reinforcement of Aspect identity. </div> </div> </div>Good point.<br /> <br /> However, it seems that Dragon-Blooded have many more means for shedding levels of anima banner than Solar Exalted do, which better allows them to step down from bonfire more often and more easily. That reduces the liability.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Eh. I'm probably fretting too much over Air's defenses. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you mean by &quot;Air&quot;.<br /> <br /> Air Aspect Dragon-Blooded are just as capable of learning Melee Charms as Fire Aspects, especially now that Dragon-Blooded get an additional two Favored Abilities. Since none of the most common Melee Charms require Air Auras, an Air Aspect is sitting pretty in the Fire Auras that those Charms will provide him. When his anima goes to bonfire and puts him into Air Aura, he may lose access to some Melee tricks, but he gains access to the Signature Melee Charm of his Aspect, and he gets another option with Mela's Flashing Tongue.<br /> <br /> He could also use his Air Aura to empower non-Melee Charms like Soaring Zephyr Flight, Horizon-Spanning Arc, Flying Whirlwind Razor, Safety Among Enemies, Elusive Crosswind Defense, the Air version of Elusive Dragon-God Dispersion, Dragon-Kin Empowerment, Elemental Burst Technique, The Wind Turns, Dragon Vortex Attack, Storm-Gathering Fervor, (Air) Protection Technique, Body-Like-Clouds Meditation, Untethered Pegasus Spirit, Cunning Beast-Mind Inspiration, Mela's Twin Fangs, Persistent Hornet Attack, Thousand Razor Wind, Whirlwind Shield Technique, and Vengeful Gust Counterstrike.<br /> <br /> Huh, apparently not any Stealth Charms at all. Mela's Hungry Jaws is the only one with the Air and Aura keywords, but it explicitly cannot be used against anyone who knows the Dragon-Blood is there, even if they can't see her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T19:18:27-07:00","id":1210231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209634-terrestrial-vs-celestial-how-big-is-the-power-gap-now?p=1210204#post1210204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what you mean by &quot;Air&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The picture gets a lot brighter once you get to Signatures and high-Essence, as you did in your examples. I'm primarily looking at the <i>survivability</i> of <i>starting</i> player characters who have an interest in maintaining Aura, and I'm not limiting myself to Melee defenses in doing so.<br /> <br /> Here's what I'm looking at. If you're under attack and are trying to defend yourself* or others without interrupting an Aura-duration Charm, at starting Essence...<br /> <br /> <i>Any</i> Aura can use the Brawl, Dodge, and Melee Excellencies, along with Flame-Borne Interception and Blinding Spark Distraction in Melee, and (Element) Protection Technique in Resistance.<br /> <br /> <i>Water</i> Aura can additionally use Blade-Deflecting Palm in Brawl, Graceful Flowing Defense in Melee, and Eternal Tide Endurance in Resistance.<br /> <br /> <i>Fire </i>Aura can additionally use Flickering Candle Meditation, Hopping Firecracker Evasion, and Ember-Amid-Smoke Misdirection in Dodge; Crossfire Flash and Flame Warden Stance from Melee; and Shimmering Heat Mirage from Stealth.<br /> <br /> <i>Earth</i> Aura can additionally use Impervious Skin of Stone and Unfeeling Earth Meditation in Resistance<br /> <br /> <i>Wood</i> Aura can additionally use Virtuous Negation Defense in Dodge and Supple Viridian Scales in Resistance<br /> <br /> <i>Air</i> Aura can additionally use... nothing.<br /> <br /> A character who wants to defend themselves at starting Essence without breaking Air Aura cannot use any Charm that they couldn't use with any other Aura. Air gains nothing whatsoever special on defense from any Ability at starting Essence. Wood also has very little; Virtuous Negation does nothing to help with attacks against you yourself, and Supple Viridian Scales is only a defense boost if you're wearing Medium+ armor, otherwise it's a utility Charm.<br /> <br /> Higher Essence does help, <i>especially</i> for Wood, since Wood Melee picks up Aura of Grasping Branches and Root-and-Hand Merging from Ess 3.<br /> <br /> *I'm defining &quot;defend yourself&quot; here as &quot;you are being attacked and need to not-die.&quot; Yes, Air has Stealth, but it's too late to hide if the arrow/daiklave/rock/whatever is already flying at your head.<br /> <hr /><br /> It occurs to me that I could also complain about high-Essence Charms whose use invalidates all their prerequisites. Revolving-Hurricane-Force Defense gives an Essence 5, Resistance-focused character an Air-elemental, Aura-duration persistent defense, but the Aura duration means that of the five Resistance Charms you must have in order to learn Revolving-Hurricane-Force, only (Element) Protection Technique can be used without ending it, rendering the other four dead weight for the duration of Revolving-Hurricane-Force.<br /> <hr /><br /> I don't think any of this is unplayable, mind you. It just makes certain Aura duration Charms feel like their real duration is &quot;until you become the target of a serious attack.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T20:03:24-07:00","id":1210244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ascension</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209634-terrestrial-vs-celestial-how-big-is-the-power-gap-now?p=1210231#post1210231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Wood</i> Aura can additionally use Virtuous Negation Defense in Dodge and Supple Viridian Scales in Resistance</div> </div> </div> </div>Virtuous Negation Defense actually puts a Dragon-Blooded into danger rather than helping them avoid it.<br /> <br /> Which means Wood is in much the same boat that Air is, which only makes sense when both of them count ranged attack Abilities as Aspect Abilities; and Air further has access to Lore's elemental projectiles and potentially also sorcerous spells. The primary defense of Wood and Air Essence is distance from the things which would hurt the Princes of the Earth. Wood additionally has the advantage of riding horses to maintain distance, and Air has Stealth.<br /> <br /> While only one Stealth Charm <i>requires</i> Air Aura, most of them are conducive to <i>remaining</i> in Air Aura.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *I'm defining &quot;defend yourself&quot; here as &quot;you are being attacked and need to not-die.&quot; Yes, Air has Stealth, but it's too late to hide if the arrow/daiklave/rock/whatever is already flying at your head. </div> </div> </div>Dodge's basic Disengage Charms are Balanced, and the Air-aspected Athletics Charm, Soaring Leap Technique, can be also be used to assist a Disengage action.<br /> <br /> So, an Air Aspect has options for retreating to the safety of distance if she's caught at close range.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T23:41:59-07:00","id":1210306,"title":"","content":"Um... Something something Martial Arts? Merit tax and all but... It <i>is</i> there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T06:22:07-07:00","id":1210384,"title":"","content":"Why is it so important for beginning characters to maintain an Air Aura for multiple turns, anyway?<br /> <br /> There aren\u2019t many Charms that require an Air Aura to keep working, and all of the ones that do are Essence 3+.<br /> <br /> Further, the Charms that have durations of \u201cAir Aura\u201d are usually the kind of Charms you can use while fighting at range with Air Thrown and Air Archery, and protecting yourself with Balanced Charms.<br /> <br /> Air Aspects have \u201cMonkey Leap Technique+\u201d as an anima power, which helps them leap atop high walls and roofs where their enemies can\u2019t easily reach them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T06:51:04-07:00","id":1210389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209634-terrestrial-vs-celestial-how-big-is-the-power-gap-now?p=1210244#post1210244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dodge's basic Disengage Charms are Balanced, and the Air-aspected Athletics Charm, Soaring Leap Technique, can be also be used to assist a Disengage action.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was there an updated version put out or something? Because the only balanced Dodge charm in my PDF is the Excellency.<br /> <br /> Even then, disengaging does bupkis against other ranged fighters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T07:39:09-07:00","id":1210412,"title":"","content":"The main defence anyway is the excellency. Making your opponent reroll 1-3 of their successes is a nice little kicker, but it\u2019s not like solars where the post excellency charms make you basically unhittable to certain opponents. <br /> <br /> I mean they\u2019re not even guaranteed to do anything, you could reroll two sevens into a 2 and a 10. Compared to just adding a straight 3 defence that\u2019s not make or break territory. It might make the difference but it won\u2019t all that often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T09:22:00-07:00","id":1210452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209634-terrestrial-vs-celestial-how-big-is-the-power-gap-now?p=1210384#post1210384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is it so important for beginning characters to maintain an Air Aura for multiple turns, anyway?<br /> <br /> There aren\u2019t many Charms that require an Air Aura to keep working, and all of the ones that do are Essence 3+.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did realize after I posted that I understated my case; maintaining Aura through to your next turn isn't only important for Aura-duration Charms, but for <i>all</i> Aura-keyworded Charms you want to use, since losing Aura on defense means you wouldn't be able to use anything Aura-powered when your turn comes up.<br /> <br /> But the other points made are fair, particularly DrLoveMonkey's comment that few of the low-level non-Excellency defensive Charms make much difference anyway. I do like Impervious Skin of Stone and Graceful Flowing Defense when used in Aura, but the rest are quite minor, unreliable, and/or situational. I'm done arguing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T09:34:38-07:00","id":1210459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ascension</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209634-terrestrial-vs-celestial-how-big-is-the-power-gap-now?p=1210452#post1210452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the other points made are fair, particularly DrLoveMonkey's comment that few of the low-level non-Excellency defensive Charms make much difference anyway. I do like Impervious Skin of Stone and Graceful Flowing Defense when used in Aura, but the rest are quite minor, unreliable, and/or situational. I'm done arguing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep! It\u2019s actualy even better since excellencies like the dodge excellency are also penalty negators. It is definitely better to be a fire aspect for dodging though, but that\u2019s the tradgedy of the terrestrial.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s okay though, the air aspects get to stick it to the fire guys in other abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T09:48:16-07:00","id":1210467,"title":"","content":"With lore and thown in-aspect air are the premier elemental bolt users.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T12:11:35-07:00","id":1210530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209634-terrestrial-vs-celestial-how-big-is-the-power-gap-now#post1209634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have happily backed the dragonblooded kickstarter and have been thrilled with everything I have read so far. I am incredibly impressed with the manuscript so far, and have tons of confidence in the new dev team.However I haven't had as much time to sit and tinker with the new Charms as I would like, and was wondering what the wise minds of this forum might think about them.<br /> <br /> So how big is the power gap between Solars and Dragonblooded now? Could something like an Essence 3 Dynast be a deadly threat to a newborn Dawn? Are the 2e days of combat specced Solars laughing in the face of dozens of Wyld Hunters long gone?<br /> <br /> Eager to hear peoples thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Solar can't fight dozens anymore, no. But the gap is massive still. 3-1 easily, in favor of the one Solar.<br /> <br /> Except for Immaculate Martial Artists, mind. And DB lore has a trick that could edge it more in DBs favor. Basically, teamwork _matters,_ as does IMA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":800,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","user":"Fenrir666","date":". 04-23-2018, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T13:12:41-07:00","id":1211116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209634-terrestrial-vs-celestial-how-big-is-the-power-gap-now?p=1210530#post1210530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Solar can't fight dozens anymore, no. But the gap is massive still. 3-1 easily, in favor of the one Solar.<br /> <br /> Except for Immaculate Martial Artists, mind. And DB lore has a trick that could edge it more in DBs favor. Basically, teamwork _matters,_ as does IMA.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Having spent some time today looking through the set I tend to agree with you, and various other posters here, particularly DrLoveMonkey (who's detailed analysis in the other thread is deeply appreciated.) I haven't had time to really dig into the Immaculate Martial Arts though yet (too busy cooing excitedly over all the new spells.) How much of an equaliser do we think these might turn out to be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T14:58:05-07:00","id":1211170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209634-terrestrial-vs-celestial-how-big-is-the-power-gap-now?p=1211116#post1211116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Having spent some time today looking through the set I tend to agree with you, and various other posters here, particularly DrLoveMonkey (who's detailed analysis in the other thread is deeply appreciated.) I haven't had time to really dig into the Immaculate Martial Arts though yet (too busy cooing excitedly over all the new spells.) How much of an equaliser do we think these might turn out to be?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They are not that much of an equalizer if we are talking about the monster Dawn white room scenario. The big punch charms still have restrictions on their use and require set up that you will never get against a super min-maxed Dawn. Two or three versus one more laid back Dawn at low essence is definitely doable.<br /> <br /> I mean Crumplepunch had 3 combat focused DBs (melee and brawl do not remember the 3rd) focus attack a supernal Resistance and he was gaining initiative even after being grappled and under control for some rounds. But then again Resistance can do that against other solars as well. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T21:12:29-07:00","id":1211285,"title":"","content":"Well, now it actually seems plausible that they killed so many solars by dog piling them instead of the entire host getting soloed by a single combat focused elder essence solar after hearing them plot against them from the other side of Creation thanks to the inevitable loose lipped idiot that didn't listen when the Sidereal said not to say anything in Creation (and then they went and slam dunked Chejop so hard he was sent to Malfeas and had to wait for time to catch up with his ass whooping).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}